{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiTowerBarParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiTowerBarParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiTowerBarParity.kappa2_rung_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiTowerBarParity.kappa2_rung_real","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OhtsukiTowerBarParity.lean#L84-L89","doc":"**First even rung `κ₂` is a volume/mass correction** (`n = 2`, `m = 1`): the\n`(i·t)²·κ₂ = −t²·κ₂` term (`κ₂ = 2π²/27`) is real, `Im = 0`. Concrete\ninstance of `even_rung_real`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiTowerBarParity.kappa1_rung_imaginary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiTowerBarParity.kappa1_rung_imaginary","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OhtsukiTowerBarParity.lean#L77-L82","doc":"**Leading odd rung `κ₁` is the bar-odd `S` carrier** (`n = 1`, `m = 0`): the\n`i·t·κ₁` term (`κ₁ = 11√3π/108`; the finite-`b` `Im 𝔙_b ≈ 0.058` scale, #3654)\nis purely imaginary, `Re = 0`. Concrete instance of `odd_rung_imaginary`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiTowerBarParity.odd_rung_imaginary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiTowerBarParity.odd_rung_imaginary","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OhtsukiTowerBarParity.lean#L62-L75","doc":"**Odd rung ⇒ imaginary ⇒ feeds `Im 𝔙 = CS` (bar-odd / decay = the c₃ `S`).**\nFor a real coefficient `κ`, the `2m+1`-th tower rung at the imaginary\nsubstrate `x = i·t` has vanishing real part: `Re((i·t)^{2m+1}·κ) = 0`.\nPairing the imaginary factors leaves one factor of `i`, so the rung is\n`((−t²)^m·t·κ)·i`, purely imaginary. So every odd Ohtsuki rung contributes to\nthe Chern–Simons / bar-odd `S` face of `𝔙`, never to the volume/mass. This is\nwhere the c₃ bar-odd sign-flip lives; the Borel resummation of exactly this\nodd sub-tower gives the exact smooth `Im 𝔙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiTowerBarParity.even_rung_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiTowerBarParity.even_rung_real","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OhtsukiTowerBarParity.lean#L50-L60","doc":"**Even rung ⇒ real ⇒ feeds `Re 𝔙 = Vol` (bar-even / mass channel).** For a\nreal coefficient `κ`, the `2m`-th tower rung at the imaginary substrate\n`x = i·t` has vanishing imaginary part: `Im((i·t)^{2m}·κ) = 0`. Pairing the\nimaginary factors via `(i·t)² = −t²` (real) leaves `(−t²)^m·κ`, a real\nnumber. So every even Ohtsuki rung contributes to the volume/mass face of\n`𝔙`, never to the bar-odd `S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiTowerBarParity.imaginary_sub_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiTowerBarParity.imaginary_sub_sq","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OhtsukiTowerBarParity.lean#L43-L48","doc":"**The paired imaginary factor is real:** `(i·t)² = −t²`, cast of a real. The\nsingle squaring that turns the imaginary substrate direction into a real\nscalar — the seed of the even/odd parity split. ","signatureChunk":0}]}